course: dictionary
lesson: 12416
title: Spots of light and shade
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words paint a picture for the reader. «Dappled» is one of them. Its clues are in the sentence: it sits next to light, shade, spots or patches. «Dappled sunlight fell through the leaves of the oak tree.» Light falling in patches, with shadow in between, is what makes the wood look dappled.
explain: Look for the picture the word helps you see. «The old grey horse was dappled with white spots.» You can picture its coat covered in spots of different shades. Dappled is not about being plain or smooth. It is about a mix of marks or patches.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «Dappled sunlight fell through the leaves» with the words «patches of light and shade». If the sentence still makes sense and gives the same picture, you have the right meaning.
fact: «Dappled» means marked with spots or patches of different colours or shades.
fact: Dappled light or shade is a pattern of light and shadow, for example under trees.
fact: A «dappled grey» horse has spotted fur.
fact: Writers use «dappled» to help the reader picture a soft, spotted pattern.
fact: Artists also use the idea of dappled light when they show light breaking into patches.
exercise: «Dappled sunlight fell through the leaves.» What does dappled mean here? | Very hot and bright all over | *Marked with patches of light and shade | Blown away by the wind | Smooth and still
exercise: A dappled grey horse has what kind of coat? | Long, wet hair | *Spotted fur in different shades | No fur at all | Smooth, plain white fur
exercise: Find and copy one word that means marked with spots or patches. | sunlight | leaves | *dappled | tree
test: «The stream was dappled with shadows from the trees.» What does dappled mean? | *Marked with patches of light and dark | Loud and fast | Deep and cold | Smooth and still
test: A painter wants to show light breaking into patches on a forest floor. Which word fits best? | Frozen | Empty | Silent | *Dappled
exam: Which picture would a writer describe as dappled? | *Sunlight patches on a forest floor | A bowl of soup | A still, dark night with no stars | A plain white wall
